# .dockerignore - Docker build-context exclusions for the account-service module
#
# Purpose:
#   Keep the Docker build context small and prevent host-side build artifacts and
#   version-control metadata from being uploaded to the Docker daemon or leaking
#   into image layers. The multi-stage Dockerfile compiles and packages the
#   application FRESH inside the Maven build stage, so nothing produced on the host
#   should ever be shipped into the context or the resulting image.
#
# Semantics:
#   Patterns are matched relative to the build-context root (the account-service/
#   directory, i.e. `docker build account-service/`). One glob pattern per line;
#   lines beginning with `#` are comments.
#
# IMPORTANT - do NOT add `pom.xml` or `src/` to this file: the Maven build stage
# in the Dockerfile requires both to resolve dependencies, compile, and package
# the executable jar. Excluding them would break the image build.

# --- Maven build output (recompiled fresh inside the build stage) ---
target/

# --- Version-control metadata ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- IDE / editor project files ---
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.settings/
.project
.classpath

# --- OS-generated files ---
.DS_Store

# --- Logs and transient output ---
*.log

# --- Docker artifacts (not needed as build inputs) ---
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# --- Documentation not required for the build ---
README.md
